<h1>OBDD</h1>
<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
(no definition here, yet, but
<a href="../terms.html#needHelp">you can help</a>.)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> ordered binary decision diagram.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="bdd.html"><em>BDD</em></a>, <a href="reducedOrderedBDD.html"><em>reduced ordered binary decision diagram</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
OBDD referred to as Oblivious ... by <strong>Lance Fortnow</strong>, <em>Review of Branching Programs and Binary Decision Diagrams: Theory and Applications</em>, SIGACT News, 33(1):7, March 2002. </em>
</p>

<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
<a href="https://doi.acm.org/10.1145/136035.136043" target="_blank">Symbolic Boolean manipulation with ordered binary-decision diagrams</a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Randal E. Bryant</strong>, <em>Graph-based algorithms for Boolean function manipulation</em>, IEEE Transactions on Computers, 35(8):677-691, August 1986.
</p>

